# What floor's core is. Every check that refuses a word in core reads this file and no other.
#
# Core is what floor ships and runs. Not `tests`, which stands a host up on purpose, and not the
# other plugins, which have no such boundary to keep.
#
# **Each directory is named from floor's own root, never from a repository's.** Two kinds of reader
# stand in different places. This repository's gates stand at the repository root and prefix
# `plugins/floor/`. Floor's own suite stands at the plugin root, and reads a planted copy of it as
# often as the real one. A list written from either place is unreadable from the other.
#
# **So it lives in the plugin and not in `bin/`.** A file under `bin/` belongs to this repository,
# and floor's suite ships to machines this repository is not on.
#
# **Eight places held this list, word for word, and two more held part of it.** Nothing made any of
# them agree, so a directory added to one left the rest green over code they had never read. One of
# the two partials was already wrong: floor's own `core_names_no_vendor` read `bin` and `lib` and
# never `hooks`, from the day it was written.
#
# **What holds this is a check inside floor, and it reads floor only.** `the_core_list_lives_in_one_file`
# refuses a second copy anywhere in the plugin. A copy written in a repository's own gates is out
# of its reach, and no gate holds that half today.
#
# A `#` line is prose. Every other line is one directory, and it starts in column zero.

bin
lib
hooks
